==Economy==
The woolen pile carpet industry in Eluru produces eco-friendly carpets.<ref>{{cite news|last1=Nagaraja|first1=G|title=Handmade carpet industry in doldrums|url=http://www.thehindu.com/todays-paper/tp-national/tp-andhrapradesh/handmade-carpet-industry-in-doldrums/article5808247.ece|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140325025836/http://www.thehindu.com/todays-paper/tp-national/tp-andhrapradesh/handmade-carpet-industry-in-doldrums/article5808247.ece|url-status=live|archive-date=25 March 2014|access-date=26 November 2015|work=The Hindu|url-access=subscription|date=20 March 2014}}</ref><ref name=encyclo>{{cite book|last1=Sajnani|first1=Manohar|title=Encyclopaedia of tourism resources in India|date=2001|publisher=Kalpaz Pub.|location=New Delhi|isbn=978-81-7835-018-9|page=66|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=nxtnsT8CdZ4C&q=Eluru&pg=PA66|access-date=26 November 2015}}</ref>

== Culture and tourism ==
[[File:Buddha Statue at Eluru.jpg|thumb|199x199px|Buddha Park at Eluru]]
There are many landmarks and tourism destinations in the district. Eluru is the largest city of the district with many destinations related to [[Buddhists]] and [[Archeologists|Archeological]] importance such as ''Guntupalli Caves'' near the city.<ref>{{cite web |title=Guntupalli caves are selected as India's top 30 heritage sites |url=http://m.indiatoday.in/story/google-world-wonders-project-archaeological-survey-of-india-asi-ministry-of-culture-heritage-monuments-maps-cultural-institute/1/344632.html}}</ref> Eluru city hosts a 74-foot high Buddha statue in the heart of the city. Some of the religious destinations include, [[Dwaraka Tirumala]] known with the name as ''Chinna Tirumala'',<ref>{{cite web |title=Lord Venkateswara Temple |url=https://www.deccanchronicle.com/151026/nation-current-affairs/article/lord-rides-suryaprabha-vahana-chinna-tirumala}}</ref> and [[Veerabhadra Temple, Pattiseema]].
[[File:Devotees near entrance of Dwaraka Tirumala temple.jpg|alt=|thumb|199x199px|[[Dwaraka Tirumala]] Temple devotees]]
[[File:Caves on Dhammalingesvarasvami Hill 03.JPG|thumb|199x199px|Caves on Dhammalingesvarasvami Hill at [[Guntupalle, Eluru district|Guntupalle]]]]

